hort-range status, notation, topology, Araki--Woods, author comments, then prose/layout [Task 2]\n675:- The current short-range redesign should use finite-support adapted symplectic coordinates, finite coordinate exhaustions `J_n`, an exact signed-pure/trace product state, direct product GNS/type analysis, and quasi-equivalence transfer only afterward. The handoff is `work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/PROOF-HANDOFF.md`. [Task 7]\n681:- symptom: author comments are hidden globally or compile success is treated as publication readiness -> cause: mathematical/content risks were conflated with TeX status -> fix: resolve each `\\\\LS`/`\\\\DS` comment by proof, citation, demotion, or removal, and retain audit risks after a successful build [Task 2][Task 3]\n759:applies_to: cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/ReplicaWormhole.github.io; reuse_rule=reuse only for this account/site arrangement; do not alter the `/homepage` project-site configuration and recheck deployment status before claiming it is live\n783:- symptom: repository configuration is pushed but redirect is declared live -> cause: API status remained `building` -> fix: poll/verify after deployment completes; only then state that the root redirect is live. [Task 1]\n841:- when the user said “Start this project” and then “Can you solve this? You can work with subagents.” -> use scoped delegated research where useful, but produce rigorous, checked artifacts with explicit assumptions, copy/gate complexity, source locators, and adversarial-review status rather than a survey or unsupported claim [Task 1][Task 2]\n1098:applies_to: cwd=<original-home>/Projects/current/homepage; reuse_rule=reuse for unpublished dictated-post work in this checkout; treat citations, claims, and publication status as draft-specific until the user directs otherwise\n1143:- The separate spec is `drafts/typed-scientific-argument-system-spec.tex`. An `ArgumentArtifact` has one primary conclusion and Lamport-addressed steps; each