{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/adversarial_review.md && git diff -- FiniteFiber/FullPauliSupportLocality.lean | sed -n '1,420p' && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"# Adversarial Review Protocol\n\nUse this before closing substantive Codex work. The goal is to find defects, not\nto summarize accomplishments.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Identify the artifact types touched: `code`, `math`, `tex`, `computation`,\n   `source-backed`, `workflow`.\n2. Inspect the diff or new artifact against the user's request.\n3. Report findings by severity first. If there are no findings, say so and state\n   the remaining risk.\n\n## Universal Checks\n\n- Did the work answer the actual latest user request?\n- Did it modify unrelated files or broaden scope?\n- Did it overwrite, reformat, or revert pre-existing user changes?\n- Are generated files, caches, logs, plots, PDFs, or build artifacts handled\n  intentionally?\n- Are final claims stronger than the evidence supports?\n- Are verification commands actually relevant to the changed artifact?\n\n## Code Checks\n\n- Does the changed behavior match the stated interface and edge cases?\n- Are tests missing for a changed behavior, bug fix, parser, numerical routine,\n  CLI command, or user-facing workflow?\n- Are errors handled where inputs, files, network calls, or external tools can\n  fail?\n- Is there hidden global state, path sensitivity, nondeterminism, race risk, or\n  stale cache behavior?\n- Did dependency, config, or environment changes alter unrelated workflows?\n\n## Math Checks\n\n- Are all assumptions, domains, signs, conventions, normalizations, and boundary\n  conditions stated before use?\n- Are definitions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n M ../AGENTS.md\n M ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/README.md\n D ../writing/.type_II_stabilizer_proof.tex.swp\n D ../writing/prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/.main.tex.swp\n?? ../.gitignore\n?? ../AristotleCandidates/\n?? ./\n?? ../project_graph.json\n?? ../project_graph.schema.json\n?? ../research/\n?? ../sources/Nielsen_Chuang.pdf\n?? ../sources/Rudin.pdf\n?? ../sources/Wilde_book.pdf\n?? ../sources/absorbtion_D3_brane.pdf\n?? ../sources/quantum-computation-and-quantum-information-nielsen-chuang.pdf\n?? ../sources/thermodynamic_irreversibility.pdf\n?? ../support_corner_stabilizer.pdf\n?? ../support_corner_stabilizer.tex\n?? ../validate_project_graph.py\n?? ../work/2026-07-topological-order-invariants/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/PROOF-HANDOFF.md\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I002-general-stabilizer-criterion/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I003-half-chain-finite-support-obstruction/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I004-ogata-surface-code-cone-algebras/\n?? ../work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I005-flat-stabilizer-support-corners-and-sector-classification/\n?? ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/\n?? ../work/AGENTS.md\n?? ../work/aristotle_autopilot/\n?? ../work/overleaf_publication_audit/\n?? ../writing/canonical_stabilizer_appendix_blueprint/\n?? ../writing/prl_stabilizer_region_algebras_canonical_appendix_draft/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
